  "_comment": "ALT-R&B drum patterns (drum-role space). Rhythm archetypes are unprotectable scenes a faire (../../docs/idiom-research/legal.md), so the named grooves are encoded plainly and provenance says which pattern each one is. Grids follow ../../docs/idiom-research/genre-funk-soul-rnb.md section C6: cross-stick rim instead of a full snare, soft kick, 16th hats with light open accents, snaps and shaker, and NO crash washes anywhere. Authored on the STRAIGHT grid -- the pack's swing (0.16, about a 54 percent shuffle) is applied downstream. The laid-back feel is a render matter, not a grid matter, exactly as with the Stax drag in the soul pack.",
